  "changes": [
    "A native side-cheek deformation carries the surrounding skin through the contour change, with cached source-space support and signed cheek-control response.",
    "Replacement cheek vertices use their existing barycentric triangle bindings to bound inward clearance. A smoothly introduced margin up to 0.3 mm prevents coplanar flicker; the outer edge remains tied to the native surface.",
    "Native cheek normals are locally averaged, and the replacement inherits those actual body normals instead of raw cage normals."
  ],
